The raw_customers table has some region values as numeric codes ('01'–'04') instead of names. raw_region_map gives an unambiguous mapping from code to name (01=WEST, 02=EAST, 03=NORTH, 04=SOUTH). The names already used (WEST, EAST, etc.) are the expected domain, so the fix is to map the codes in silver_customers using a left join to the map and fall back to the upper-cased region when no code matches.

The map has exactly 4 rows with unique codes, so the join cannot duplicate customers. The row count and the columns stay the same.

{"diagnosis": "Some raw_customers rows carry numeric region codes (01-04) instead of region names; raw_region_map gives the authoritative code-to-name mapping. silver_customers should translate the codes to names.", "decision": "fix", "confidence": 0.93, "pre_sql": [], "step_overrides": {"silver_customers": "CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE silver_customers AS SELECT c.customer_id, upper(COALESCE(m.region_name, c.region)) AS region FROM raw_customers c LEFT JOIN raw_region_map m ON trim(c.region) = m.region_code"}}
